    "Most carriers start as non-career city carrier assistants or rural carrier associates and convert to career positions over time. Hiring requires an online assessment, a background check, a drug screen and a safe driving record. Postal jobs offer federal benefits and a steady career, though new carriers often work long, irregular hours."
